From e481eb03b0f91afc82cf4c17e474ce33f6072229 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:09:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel material properties: fixes from a review

- the variant with strides did not compile with the runtime checks
  disabled (`mfront_errno_old` declared only with the checks);
- SYCL backend: the device memory was never freed (empty destructor of
  the data buffers); the extents of the strided fields were too large;
  the values between the values of a strided output were overwritten
  when the output was copied back;
- the array of the pointers to the arguments, generally on the stack of
  the calling code, was read in the kernels. The pointers are copied in
  the kernels, one by one: nvc++ 25.11 does not map an array of pointers
  captured by a lambda in an OpenMP target region;
- the data transfers are made inside the `try` block, so that their
  exceptions do not cross the boundary of the C function;
- the name of the backend is part of the header guard;
- the bounds and the default values of the parameters are written with
  14 significant digits;
- grid size of the CUDA kernels, error message of a negative stride,
  unused variables, copies of the generators of the factory, and a stray
  copy of a source file removed.

The material property test of the openmp-host-gcc configuration also
compiles a material property with the runtime checks disabled.
